	(text "Power: +5V_CABLE / VBUS in -> U5 mux -> +5V. U1 TPS79901 3V3, U4 TPS7A2033 3V3_D, U3 LT8365 APD bias (100-220 V) -> APD_BIAS."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 20 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "080e0e57-0b5a-45a9-aec9-6ea27582a186")
	)
	(text "Design intent (Rev A, revision 3; nothing here is simulated or measured; details and citations in\n    docs/schematic/power.md)\nPROPOSED  +5V (U5 OUT) entry: C1 10 uF + C2 100 nF.\nPROPOSED  U1 TPS79901: VOUT = 1.193 V x (1 + R1/R2) = 3.316 V nominal (R1 17.8k, R2 10.0k). CFB 1 nF\n    (see note).\nVERIFIED  TPS79901 CFB is required for stability; 3 pF to 1 nF when R1||R2 = 250k; <5 pF for fast\n    start (SBVS056L p.14, 8.2.2.6).\nUNRESOLVED  Here R1||R2 = 6.4k, not 250k: the datasheet range was not stated for this impedance; 1\n    nF is a PROPOSED value.\nPROPOSED  3V3 load estimate (rev 2): OPA857 26.8 mA max + OPA855 19.5 mA max (IQ 17.8 typ, 16-19.5\n    mA at VS = 5 V, OPA855 SBOS622D PDF p.7; Fig 6-27 p.12 shows about 16-17.5 mA at 3.3 V, so 19.5\n    is conservative) + TLV3605 17.5 mA max + OPA2320 ~2 mA = about 66 mA. U1 TPS79901 is rated 200\n    mA. PROPOSED, not measured.\nREMOVED  (decision 12) U2 LM27762 +/-3V7, 5V_A bead/caps, PGOOD_VGA and TP1: the VCA821 VGA is gone,\n    the OPA855 runs from 3V3.\nPROPOSED  U3 LT8365 values per docs/calculations/apd-bias-design.md sections 3.2 and 4: 500 kHz (RT\n    84.5k), L1 10 uH, boost to ~110 V + doubler.\nVERIFIED  SYNC/MODE: float = pulse-skip, GND = Burst, 100k to GND = Burst/SSFM (LT8365 Rev. A p.7).\n    BIAS tie to GND if unused; INTVCC 1 uF (p.7).\nPROPOSED  EN/UVLO 200k/200k from 5V_HVIN, always connected. Q3 DMN2056U-7 pulls EN/UVLO to GND = HV\n    OFF. Gate = HV_DIS, R33 100k pull-up to 3V3_D, R34 1k series: HV is OFF until the ESP32 drives\n    HV_DIS low after verifying the DAC (decision 11). J1 HV FORCE ON (DNP) shorts the gate to GND\n    for bench use without firmware.\nPROPOSED  U4 TPS7A2033 3V3_D: 300 mA, radio must stay disabled; load est. 60 mA\n    (docs/research/module-controller.md). CIN 1 uF, COUT 10 uF + 1 uF (datasheet minimum 1 uF, max\n    200 uF: SBVS338H p.5).\nPROPOSED  BIAS: R28 0R to GND fitted; R29 0R to 5V_HVIN DNP. Fit exactly one of them. SYNC options\n    R26/R27/TP2 are DNP.\nPROPOSED  D2 (GND to SW, from the p.30 250 V example, purpose not stated) is DNP. Q1/Q2 clamp ~150\n    uA. C8 and R19 form filter stage 1.\nPROPOSED  HV_MON = HV_OUT/101 (R20+R32 10M, R21 100k): 1.39 V at 140 V. Stage 2 filter (10k + 10 nF)\n    is on the front-end sheet.\nNet names: HV_V1, HV_PUMP, HV_RAW, HV_OUT, HV_CLAMP, 5V_HVIN, EN, SYNC, BIAS, RT, SS, VC, FBX are\n    local labels; APD_BIAS = HV_FILT.\nHierarchical pins: in +5V_CABLE, VBUS, DAC_HV, HV_DIS; out 3V3, 3V3_D, APD_BIAS, HV_MON, PWR_SRC.\nPROPOSED  (decision 13, revision 3) U5 TPS2121RUXR: IN1 pin 7 = +5V_CABLE (priority), IN2 pin 2 =\n    VBUS (USB-C), OUT pins 1 and 8 = +5V (internal merged rail for U1, U3 via L2, U4); GND pin 12;\n    CP2 pin 3 = GND. Pin numbers match the TPS2121 pin table (SLVSEA3F p.4-5, the symbol's ILM is\n    the datasheet ILIM).\nPROPOSED  Priority: PR1 from +5V_CABLE through R35 294k / R36 100k: cable selected above about\n    3.98-4.33 V rising, dropped below about 3.90-4.10 V (SLVSEA3F p.7-8 VREF 0.99-1.10 V, p.18 Table\n    9-3). UNRESOLVED: chatter near the threshold with a real ULX3S rail (hysteresis only about 0.08\n    V on the rail).\nPROPOSED  Overvoltage: OV1 R39 464k / R40 100k from +5V_CABLE, OV2 R41 464k / R42 100k from VBUS;\n    trip about 5.6-6.2 V, below the TPS799 7.0 V abs max (SBVS056L p.4); OV pin range 0-5.5 V\n    (SLVSEA3F p.6).\nVERIFIED  ST (pin 9): R37 10k pull-up to 3V3_D, PWR_SRC high = cable (or OUT Hi-Z), low = USB\n    (SLVSEA3F p.18); pull-up range 6-20k p.6.\nPROPOSED  ILM R38 100k (maximum RILM; ILM = 65.2/RILM^0.861 = 1.24 A typ, p.13). UNRESOLVED: the\n    datasheet table has no 100k row (1.5 A typ at 80k, p.8), so the minimum limit is not stated. SS\n    C32 220 nF (about 350-400 V/s, p.13 Table 9-1 scaled, estimate); first-plug settling and inrush\n    UNRESOLVED until measured. The limit protects U5 and the cable; it does not enforce the 0.5 A\n    USB budget.\nPROPOSED  C33 4.7 uF 0805 on +5V_CABLE at IN1, C34 4.7 uF 0805 on VBUS at IN2 (TI recommends a\n    larger input capacitor to damp cable ringing, SLVSEA3F p.33); C1/C2 stay on +5V (OUT).\n    UNRESOLVED: USB attach capacitance limit not checked against the USB spec. No TVS (24 V abs max\n    p.6), no other reverse protection (keyed connector).\nPROPOSED  No back-feed (fast reverse blocking, <= 1 uA leakage, SLVSEA3F p.7, p.15): both present\n    means cable powers and USB carries data only. Switchover about 100 us typ (tSW p.7); hold-up\n    droop about 1 V estimated, not measured.\nPROPOSED  ERC: U5 OUT pins 1 and 8 are power_out on the +5V net, so +5V needs no PWR_FLAG; the root\n    PWR_FLAG #FLG04 sits on +5V_CABLE. Budget about 0.19 A worst case (docs/research/usb-standalone-\n    power.md section 1.5, estimate); radio must stay disabled. USB-alone firmware starts HV at the\n    low-bias end in steps (PROPOSED)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 308 28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "49163317-eef8-4aa8-918e-2a646ab2094b")
	)
	(text "HV WARNING\nAPD bias reaches 220 V. Stored energy ~2.3 mJ (docs/calculations/apd-bias-design.md section 4). Can\n    be hazardous.\nNever probe HV_OUT, HV_RAW, HV_PUMP, HV_V1 or HV_CLAMP directly. Use HV_MON (HV_OUT/101) for\n    observation.\nCapacitors C5-C8, C25 and resistors R19, R30 carry >= 200 V ratings; keep 200 V creepage/clearance\n    on every HV_ net,\nseries-limited, with the HV netclass 1.0 mm clearance. Keep the APD_BIAS/FBX area away from TIA_IN.\nHV is OFF by default (Q3 gate pulled up); J1 FORCE ON overrides the firmware disable: fit only on\n    the bench with the DAC set. Discharge through the divider takes ~0.5 s: wait before touching.\nReferences: LT8365 Rev. A datasheet p.30 (250 V example), DC2838A demo manual Rev. 0."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
